     base_link origin = centre of the body underside (same as the asset manifest); ground is z = -ground_clearance.
     MECANUM: wheels are plain continuous joints about +y with cylinder collisions of the true 45 mm width. There are no roller
     links. Roller behaviour must come from the simulator: (a) kinematic: a mecanum drive plugin/controller with the X-pattern
     inverse kinematics w_i = (vx + k_i vy + (lx+ly) kz_i wz)/r, k=(-1,+1,+1,-1), kz=(-1,+1,-1,+1) for FL,FR,RL,RR
     (gz-sim MecanumDrive system, ros2_control mecanum_drive_controller); (b) dynamic: anisotropic friction per wheel with
     mu2 ~ 0 along the ground-contact roller axis a_i=(sin45, s_i cos45), s=(-1,+1,+1,-1) (FL,FR,RL,RR), as CRANE does with its
     ArticulationBody rover. The roller sign of each wheel is repeated in its <link> comment.
